摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"CarryOn context folding (arXiv:2610.18784) for DeepSeek Harness: keep what the agent established, not the whole transcript.","id":"gh:1443909174","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-carryon","slug":"xuan-tu-ai/dsh-carryon","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"CarryOn context folding (arXiv:2610.18784) for DeepSeek Harness: keep what the agent established, no"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"t the whole transcript."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"dsh-carryon"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"CarryOn context folding for DeepSeek Harness: long agent sessions keep what they established, not th"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"ding for DeepSeek Harness: long agent sessions keep what they established, not the whole transcript."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"English · 简体中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"When a DeepSeek Harness (dsh) session grows long, dsh compacts it\nby summarizing old turns into free"},{"id":"p5s2","text":" text. dsh-carryon replaces that step with **CarryOn** from\n*Pack Light, CarryOn*. Old turns are fol"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"ded into small, versioned records of\nwhat the agent has established (\"carriers\") and an execution co"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"ntext: the task, open obligations and the next step.\nEach fold is validated before it is committed, "},{"id":"p5s5","text":"and a rejected fold changes nothing."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5f4a6889-5cf6-41a4-aff1-327a9d5d6b7b"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"CarryOn demo by the paper's authors. Also on the project page."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"The CarryOn runtime, from the paper. In dsh-carryon, dsh decides when to fold and keeps the recent t"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"urns; the Grounder is not ported yet (details)."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Configuration · How it works · Development · Benchmark · Troubleshooting · Releasing · Changelog"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Highlights"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"- **Drop-in backend.** dsh-carryon replaces dsh's compaction in the terminal, headless, SDK and ACP "},{"id":"p11s2","text":"profiles. dsh\nkeeps its trigger, its verbatim tail and its safety checks, and `/compact` works as be"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"fore.\n- **CarryOn mode in the Web UI.** The plugin adds a mode next to Standard mode, so you can com"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"pare both in the same\napp.\n- **Validated folds.** A fold that fails validation leaves the session un"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"touched. Rescans then back off as in the\npaper. Close to the context limit, a failed fold falls back"},{"id":"p11s6","text":" to dsh's own summary, so the session can go on.\n- **Resumable.** Fold state is stored as readable J"},{"id":"p11s7","text":"SON in the session log and restored on resume.\n- **Ported, not reinvented.** The runtime is a TypeSc"},{"id":"p11s8","text":"ript port of carrycode,\nchecked case by case against its parity fixtures."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"The checkpoint holds every carrier and the execution context. dsh keeps the most recent turns verbat"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"im after it.\nA fold costs one Tracker call, plus one Compiler call when the Tracker asks for compila"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"tion; dsh's own compaction\nmakes one summary call. The engine, the state format and how this port di"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"ffers from the paper are described in\nHow it works."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Results reported in the paper"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"These results come from the paper (Lu, McAuley, Zhang, 2026), with Claude Opus 4.7 as the agent. dsh"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"-carryon has not\nbeen benchmarked against them."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"OSWorld 2.0. CarryOn improves both binary and partial scores of the same Claude Opus 4.7 agent\nwhile"},{"id":"p17s2","text":" cutting cost per task by 35.9%. Figure from the paper's authors."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Context and cost over agent turns on OSWorld 2.0. The baseline's input context keeps growing past\n20"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"0K tokens, while CarryOn's stays near 65K. Figure from the paper's authors."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"On BrowseComp-Plus, the paper reports accuracy rising from 49.0% to 56.0% with 22.9% fewer tokens pe"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"seComp-Plus, the paper reports accuracy rising from 49.0% to 56.0% with 22.9% fewer tokens per task."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"You need dsh **0.2.2-alpha.3** (each dsh-carryon release supports\nexactly one dsh release), Node.js "},{"id":"p21s2","text":"24.9 or later (dsh's own requirement), and pnpm on your `PATH`\n(`npm install -g pnpm`), which `dsh p"},{"id":"p21s3","text":" (dsh's own requirement), and pnpm on your `PATH`\n(`npm install -g pnpm`), which `dsh plugin` calls."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Install the plugin into the profile you use. For the terminal UI:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"For the Web UI:"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"If dsh 0.2.2-alpha.3 is already installed globally, drop the `npx @deepseek-ai/dsh@0.2.2-alpha.3` pr"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"efix, for example\n`dsh plugin --profile tui add dsh-carryon`. The same goes for the commands below."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Restart dsh: `npx @deepseek-ai/dsh@0.2.2-alpha.3` opens the terminal UI, and\n`npx @deepseek-ai/dsh@0"},{"id":"p27s2","text":".2.2-alpha.3 web` serves the Web UI and prints its address. In the terminal UI, every compaction is "},{"id":"p27s3","text":"now a CarryOn fold. In the Web UI, new sessions start in\n**CarryOn mode**, which you can switch from"},{"id":"p27s4","text":" the mode menu next to the chat box:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"### Check, update, remove"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"`dsh plugin` passes its arguments to pnpm in the profile's directory, so pnpm's commands work. Check"},{"id":"p29s2","text":" that the plugin\nis installed:"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"In the Web UI it is also listed under **Plugins → Installed plugins**. Once the session is long enou"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"gh to compact\n(or after `/compact`), a fold's checkpoint appears where dsh shows a compaction summar"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"y, and its full state is under\nTrajectory → Raw Output."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"Update to the latest release for your dsh version:"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"Remove it:"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"Use `--profile web` for the Web UI. Something not working? See Troubleshooting."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"The plugin's config row is `carryon-compaction`. It accepts dsh's own compaction keys (`thresholdRat"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"io`,\n`retainTokens`, …) and a few CarryOn keys. For example, put this in `$DSH_HOME/profiles/tui/cor"},{"id":"p38s3","text":"dis.patch.yml` to fold at\nhalf of the context window and run the CarryOn roles on the cheaper `deeps"},{"id":"p38s4","text":"ml` to fold at\nhalf of the context window and run the CarryOn roles on the cheaper `deepseek-flash`:"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"dsh replaces a row's whole `config` with the patched one, so list all your keys together. See\nConfig"},{"id":"p40s2","text":"uration for every key, the defaults, and the Web UI's limits."},{"id":"p41s1","text":"## Citation"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"dsh-carryon implements the method of this paper. If you use it in research, please cite the paper:"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"carrycode and dsh-carryon are independent reimplementations built from the paper. They are not affil"},{"id":"p44s2","text":"iated with the\npaper's authors or with DeepSeek."},{"id":"p45s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p46s1","text":"dsh-carryon's code is Apache-2.0. The demo video and the figures shown above belong to the paper's a"},{"id":"p46s2","text":"uthors,\nwho gave permission to show them here; they are not covered by that license."}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
